flowchart LR
    %% Cache/memory layout v2. Logical tiers share one physical UMA budget.
    subgraph UMA["ONE physical 32 GiB LPDDR pool: Core Ultra 7 258V + Arc 140V"]
        PIN["Pinned if budget permits: embedding, attention, router, shared/dense, head"]
        HOT["Hot per-layer expert arena: GPU-readable, native OTD LRU"]
        WARM["Warm: host DRAM / OS page cache; NOT extra RAM"]
        STAGE["Bounded staging / USM / transform buffers"]
        KV["KV U4 + prefix pages + C1/C2/C4 slot state"]
        DRAFT["MTP or DFlash draft weights and state, only when enabled"]
        OS["OS, runtime, activations and safety headroom"]
    end

    subgraph BACKING["Separate physical NVMe storage"]
        STORE["Cold immutable packed expert weights, checksums and offsets"]
    end

    subgraph ACCESS["Native OTD baseline; experimental scheduling is gated"]
        TARGET["Target verifier demand, highest priority"]
        DREQ["Drafter demand if its own MoE backend uses OTD"]
        PF["Speculative prefetch, bounded, proposed"]
        READ["Positional read, scale/ZP transforms and GPU copy"]
        KEY["Residency key: checkpoint, layer, expert, projection, quant profile"]
        EXEC["Actual supported GPU kernel"]
    end

    subgraph CONTROL["Admission and accounting"]
        BUDGET["Unique physical bytes: OS + pinned + hot + warm + staging + KV + draft + margin"]
        SHRINK["On pressure: shrink draft window, cache or slots; then plain; never OS thrash"]
        TRACE["Trace: route, hit/miss, IO bytes, accepted/committed, p95 TTFT/TPOT"]
    end

    STORE --> READ
    TARGET --> READ
    DREQ --> READ
    PF -.->|only after priority and cancellation gate| READ
    READ --> STAGE --> HOT
    WARM -.->|optional page-cache reuse, no guaranteed hit| STAGE
    KEY --> HOT --> EXEC
    PIN --> EXEC
    KV --> BUDGET
    DRAFT --> BUDGET
    HOT --> BUDGET
    WARM --> BUDGET
    STAGE --> BUDGET
    PIN --> BUDGET
    OS --> BUDGET
    BUDGET -->|insufficient headroom| SHRINK
    EXEC --> TRACE
    READ --> TRACE
    SHRINK --> TRACE

    classDef native fill:#e9f3ff,stroke:#376ca8,color:#10283f
    classDef proposed fill:#fff1d7,stroke:#ad7822,color:#3c2b10,stroke-dasharray:5 4
    classDef memory fill:#e8f3e8,stroke:#42764a,color:#173b1d
    class TARGET,READ,EXEC native
    class DREQ,PF,KEY,BUDGET,SHRINK,TRACE proposed
    class PIN,HOT,WARM,STAGE,KV,DRAFT,OS,STORE memory
